● Plan by Problem Area                                                                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                                                                                
  A. Statistical Corrector (SC) — Highest Priority

  SC now has 3 bias + 4 GEHL tables. Training issues partially addressed.

  1. Fix SC training — Current tage_correct approach causes weight saturation and cross-workload regression. Needs: proper centering (TAGE vote in sum), dynamic PC-indexed
  thresholds (32 entries), selective training gate (train when mispred OR |sum| <= threshold + margin)
  2. GEHL tables — DONE (4 GEHL tables with geometric history lengths 4-64, 512 entries each)                                                                                                                                                      
  3. Reduce extra cycle overhead — SC forces extra_cycle every block with branches (770K extra cycles on gcc). Only force when SC actually overrode, not every block
  4. TAGE-SC chooser — Use TAGE confidence (newly_alloc, provider depth) to gate SC overrides. When TAGE is high-confidence and SC is low-confidence, trust TAGE                
  5. IMLI (Priority 2) — Inner-most loop iteration counter as an SC component                                                                                                   
                                                                                                                                                                                
  Reference: Samsung ISCA 2020 for practical hashed multi-table perceptron design. sc_overrider_lessons.md for what went wrong.                                                 
                                                                                                                                                                                
  B. TAGE Core Accuracy                                                                                                                                                         
    
  Incremental accuracy improvements to the base predictor.                                                                                                                      
    
  1. History length series — DONE (QUADRATIC, SUPEREXP, ROS in SweepTableConfig). Result: no VFS improvement over GEOMETRIC on 8 tables.
  2. Multi-entry allocation (NNN=2) — DONE (Alloc2Config, Alloc2NCConfig). Result: hurt gcc, no multi-trace win.
  3. u-bit confidence gating — DONE (AllocConfGateConfig). Result: no effect with CTR_WIDTH=1.
  Also implemented: probabilistic start (AllocProbStartConfig), partial update (PartialUpdateConfig), silent update elimination, per-table tag widths (GradedTag, StepTag, LogTag).                              
  4. Alt prediction improvements — Extended alt selection (ctr=0 OR ctr=1), 256-entry chooser indexed by hit_bank_chunk/alt_confidence/etc                                      
  5. Larger bimodal for web/JS traces (currently 4096, RUNLTS uses 128K)                                                                                                        
  6. Thrashing detection (RUNLTS) — Dynamically throttle allocation rate, zero extra storage                                                                                    
                                                                                                                                                                                
  C. Overrider Coordination                                                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                                                                                
  How SC, loop predictor, and TAGE interact.                                                                                                                                    
    
  1. Skip TAGE allocation on loop/SC hits — When overrider is correct, don't waste TAGE entries. Easy to implement in TageImpl                                                  
  2. Loop predictor: once selected = final — Don't let SC override loop predictions. Loop is highest-confidence component
  3. Set u-bit of alternate bank — When alt correctly predicts and hit bank doesn't, protect the alt entry                                                                      
                                                                                                                                                                                
  D. Latency / Energy / Architecture                                                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                                                                                
  Hardware cost optimization.                                                                                                                                                   
    
  1. P2 latency reduction — Currently 1.87 (ceil=2). Getting P2 < 1.0 (ceil=1) would be a massive VFS step change but very aggressive. Would require fundamental changes to     
  predict2 critical path
  2. Bank interleaving (EV8-style) — 4-way for single-ported SRAM, 3.3x area reduction, 2x energy reduction                                                                     
  3. Eliminate second read at retire — Checkpoint provider+counter state at prediction, skip re-read on correct predictions. ~50% fewer predictor accesses                      
  4. BR_P_ENTRY>1 — Multiple branches per entry (N-style). Plan exists, confirmed legal by organizers. Saves energy (one RAM read covers multiple branches) but significant     
  implementation effort                                                                                                                                                         
                                                                                                                                                                                
  E. Shelved / Experimental                                                                                                                                                     
    
  Not worth pursuing unless fundamentals change.                                                                                                                                
    
  - Ahead mode — Old implementations deleted (2026-04-02). New design planned as separate predictor (see 04_02_ahead_arch.md).                                                                                                  
  - Register-value-aware SC (RUNLTS) — Requires register state visibility, unclear if allowed
  - Mini-BranchNet (CNN-based) — 4-cycle latency, exotic                                                                                                                        
  - Branch precomputation — Requires separate thread, out of scope                                                                                                              
                                                                                                                                                                                
  Recommended Execution Order                                                                                                                                                   
                                                                                                                                                                                
  Phase 1: Fix SC (A1, A3-A4) — unblocks the biggest feature (A2 GEHL done)
  Phase 2: TAGE accuracy (B4-B6) + overrider coordination (C1-C2) — incremental gains, low risk (B1-B3 done)
  Phase 3: Sweep combined config on 20 traces — find VFS-optimal point
  Phase 4: Ahead TAGE (new separate predictor) — biggest VFS lever (P2 ceil 2->1)
  Phase 5: Energy/latency (D1-D2) if there's headroom, BR_P_ENTRY>1 (D4) if time permits  
